      <h2 id="buying-guide">How to Choose a CRM for Your Small Business</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Step 1 — Start free:</strong> HubSpot Free, Zoho Free, and Freshsales Free all support 3 users. Import your contacts and run the CRM for 2 weeks before paying.</li>
        <li><strong>Step 2 — Define your primary user:</strong> If the primary user is a salesperson, Pipedrive or Monday Sales CRM. If it's a marketing team, HubSpot. If it's a solo founder, HubSpot Free or Freshsales Free.</li>
        <li><strong>Step 3 — Check integrations:</strong> Verify that your email provider (Gmail/Outlook), calendar, accounting, and marketing tools have native integrations or reliable Zapier connections.</li>
        <li><strong>Step 4 — Calculate cost at scale:</strong> At 10 users, the difference between $14 and $20/user/month is $720/year. Model 1-year and 3-year costs.</li>
        <li><strong>Step 5 — Plan for growth headroom:</strong> If you expect to exceed 50 users or need enterprise features (territory management, custom objects), HubSpot Professional or Salesforce Starter are safer long-term bets.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Learn more about our <a href="/how-we-test/">testing methodology</a> and <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>.</p>

      <h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        <details>
          <summary>What is the best CRM for small business in 2026?</summary>
          <p>HubSpot CRM is the best CRM for small business in 2026 because the free tier includes contact management, email tracking, meeting scheduling, and live chat — features that competitors charge for. The Starter plan at $20/month adds automation and ad management. For sales-focused teams, Pipedrive is a strong alternative with a visual pipeline at $14/month.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Is there a free CRM for small business?</summary>
          <p>Yes. HubSpot CRM Free includes unlimited contacts, email tracking, meeting links, live chat, and basic automation — with no time limit. Zoho CRM Free supports up to 3 users with 5,000 records. Freshsales Free supports up to 3 users. For a solo founder or team under 3 people, these free tiers are genuinely usable.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How much does a CRM cost for a small business?</summary>
          <p>A CRM for small business costs between $0 (HubSpot Free, Zoho Free) and $50/user/month (HubSpot Professional). Most small businesses pay $14–$25/user/month for a mid-tier plan that includes automation, reporting, and integrations. At 5 users, expect $70–$125/month total. The key is to start free and upgrade only when you hit feature limits.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Is HubSpot or Salesforce better for small business?</summary>
          <p>HubSpot is better for small business because its free tier and $20/month Starter plan are designed for teams under 50 people. Salesforce Starter at $25/user/month is powerful but designed for larger teams with a sales operations function. For small businesses without a dedicated CRM administrator, HubSpot is easier to set up and maintain.</p>
        </details>
      </div>

